Run transition-blocks under validate_result = false.

Three changes, all following from the semantics the other clients are held to:

Block signatures now go through SkipBlockSignatureOnly (added by 0001) instead
of upstream's hand-rolled BlockSignatureVerifier pass followed by
NoVerification. That pass verified the entire block including its signature,
which is the one signature this mode must ignore; dropping it also drops the
assertion on the indexed-attestation cache it primed.

The post-block tree hash and the state-root comparison are commented out rather
than deleted, next to the reason, because they are the natural thing to re-enable
when validate_result = true is wanted.

The assertion that slot processing leaves every cache primed is downgraded to a
debug line. It holds for states lighthouse itself produced, but the pre-states
here are raw SSZ from consensus-spec-tests and complete_state_advance does not
always leave the caches built for them. The caches are rebuilt immediately
below, so the transition result is unaffected -- only the assertion is.
